    multinomial NAMED-AND-UNGATED. S0-S4 queued - currently held
    behind the R/C-division principle review.
  multinomial-counts-mutation: multinomial BART cannot mutate its
    RESPONSE side - alone among the families it cannot serve as a
    conditional inside a larger Gibbs sampler. The response is the
    combiner-owned counts_ matrix, so the content is a new COUNTS and
    n x K OFFSET channel plus creation-side surface. Enables
    competing-risks discrete-time hazard (moves with
    survival-followups), nominal-response IRT and discrete choice,
    SUR-style composition past the multinomial boundary. The
    predictor channel is already open; the gap is response-side only.
    SCHEDULED, no research gate; plan at
    docs/plans/multinomial-counts-mutation.md (5 slices; channel
    stays dbarts:::-only, public surface a recorded door). Queued
    after the multiforest arc, BEFORE the dbarts.h reshape so the C
    surface mirrors the final mutation shape.
  negbin-real-dispersion: recorded door out of the negative-binomial
    landing (docs/plans/negative-binomial.md; design sec 2 carries fork
    B's spec). Real-valued dispersion needs a non-integer-shape
    Polya-Gamma draw, for which no exact sampler exists, so shipping it
    means dbarts' first documented-approximate family (truncated
    gamma-sum, bias bounded ~1e-3 at K = 200) behind an explicit
    opt-in; the same decision gates weighted-binary's fractional
    weights. The engine seams are in place. Poisson family and grouped
    NB are companion doors (design sec 7). decision-gated.
  python-bindings: post kernel-cleanups the engine is R-free below the
    bridge, so a pybind11 facade wrapper is prototype-scale. Horizon,
    likely out-of-repo. Two contracts a non-R host would have to take
    over: host-side ingestion validation (CSC structure, categorical
    bounds, sparse metadata assembly) lives in the R bridge, and
    mixed/CSC stores hold lifetime borrows anchored by R protection.
    decision-gated.
